IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa8-helpers`
IMPORT `coa8-part14-authorisation`

-- coa8-part14-remedies.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 14, ss 369 to 373: remedies for an unauthorised donation or
-- expenditure (lines 4737-4804 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- The directors' liability to the company (s 369) is the company's right; the shareholder action (ss 370 to 373) is
-- the right of an authorised group of members to enforce it in the company's name (see "Jural relations" in NOTES.md).

§ `Remedies in case of unauthorised donations or expenditure`

-- ---- s 369: liability of directors -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4739 | (1) This section applies where a company has made a political donation or incurred political expenditure without the authorisation required by this Part.
@ref s 369(1) Where section 369 applies (src:4739)
GIVEN `the company has made a political donation or incurred political expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the donation or expenditure was authorised as this Part requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 369(1) section 369 applies` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company has made a political donation or incurred political expenditure without the authorisation required by this Part"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the authorisation answer is not known
    `s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `the company has made a political donation or incurred political expenditure`) (`s 362 helper the opposite answer` `the donation or expenditure was authorised as this Part requires`)

-- src:4749 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3)(b) a “relevant holding company” means a company that, at the time the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred—
-- src:4750 | (a) was a holding company of the company by which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred,
-- src:4751 | (b) was a UK-registered company, and
-- src:4752 | (c) was not a subsidiary of another UK-registered company.
@ref s 369(4) Relevant holding company (src:4749-4752)
GIVEN `s 1159(1) the company by which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred is a subsidiary of the other company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1158 the other company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(1) the other company is a subsidiary of another UK-registered company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 369(4) the other company is a relevant holding company` MEANS
    -- the same three limbs as s 366(4); the text of the two definitions is identical
    `s 366(4) the other company is a relevant holding company`
        `s 1159(1) the company by which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred is a subsidiary of the other company`
        `s 1158 the other company is a UK-registered company`
        `s 1159(1) the other company is a subsidiary of another UK-registered company`

-- src:4743 | (3) The directors in default are—
-- src:4744 | (a) those who, at the time the unauthorised donation was made or the unauthorised expenditure was incurred, were directors of the company by which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred, and
-- src:4745 | (b) where—
-- src:4746 | (i) that company was a subsidiary of a relevant holding company, and
-- src:4747 | (ii) the directors of the relevant holding company failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the donation being made or the expenditure being incurred,
-- src:4748 | the directors of the relevant holding company.
@ref s 369(3) The directors in default (src:4743-4748)
GIVEN `s 379(1) the person was a director of the company by which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred at the time it was made or incurred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 369(4) the company was a subsidiary of a relevant holding company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 379(1) the person was a director of that relevant holding company at that time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the relevant holding company failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the donation being made or the expenditure being incurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 369(3) the person is one of the directors in default` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors in default are— (a) those who ... were directors of the company ... and (b) ... the directors of the relevant holding company"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a director answer (section 250 or 251) or a subsidiary answer (section 1159) is not known
    `s 362 helper either answer`
        `s 379(1) the person was a director of the company by which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred at the time it was made or incurred`
        (`s 362 helper both answers` `s 369(4) the company was a subsidiary of a relevant holding company`
            (`s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `the directors of the relevant holding company failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the donation being made or the expenditure being incurred`)
                `s 379(1) the person was a director of that relevant holding company at that time`))

-- src:4740 | (2) The directors in default are jointly and severally liable—
-- src:4741 | (a) to make good to the company the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure, with interest, and
-- src:4742 | (b) to compensate the company for any loss or damage sustained by it as a result of the unauthorised donation or expenditure having been made.
@ref s 369(2) Joint and several liability of the directors in default (src:4740-4742)
GIVEN `s 369(1) section 369 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 369(3) the person is one of the directors in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 369(2) the person is jointly and severally liable to make good and to compensate the company` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where" and "The directors in default are jointly and severally liable"
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 369(1) section 369 applies` `s 369(3) the person is one of the directors in default`

-- src:4757 | (6) Where only part of a donation or expenditure was unauthorised, this section applies only to so much of it as was unauthorised.
@ref s 369(6) Only the unauthorised part (src:4757)
GIVEN `the amount of the donation or expenditure` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it that was authorised` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 369(6) the amount of the donation or expenditure to which this section applies` MEANS
    max 0 (`the amount of the donation or expenditure` MINUS `the part of it that was authorised`)

-- src:4741 | (a) to make good to the company the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure, with interest, and
@ref s 369(2)(a) The amount to make good to the company (src:4741)
GIVEN `the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount already made good to the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 369(2)(a) the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure still to be made good to the company` MEANS
    max 0 (`the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure` MINUS `the amount already made good to the company`)

-- src:4742 | (b) to compensate the company for any loss or damage sustained by it as a result of the unauthorised donation or expenditure having been made.
@ref s 369(2)(b) Compensation for loss or damage (src:4742)
GIVEN `the loss or damage sustained by the company as a result of the unauthorised donation or expenditure having been made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 369(2)(b) the amount to compensate the company for loss or damage` MEANS
    max 0 `the loss or damage sustained by the company as a result of the unauthorised donation or expenditure having been made`

-- src:4753 | (5) The interest referred to in subsection (2)(a) is interest on the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure, so far as not made good to the company—
-- src:4754 | (a) in respect of the period beginning with the date when the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred, and
-- src:4755 | (b) at such rate as the Secretary of State may prescribe by regulations.
@ref s 369(5) The amount on which interest runs (src:4753-4755)
GIVEN `the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount made good to the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 369(5) the amount on which interest runs` MEANS
    max 0 (`the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure` MINUS `the amount made good to the company`)

-- src:4754 | (a) in respect of the period beginning with the date when the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred, and
@ref s 369(5)(a) The date from which interest runs (src:4754)
-- "Section 379(2) ... does not apply for the purposes of this subsection" (line 4756): the date is the day the donation was made or the
-- expenditure incurred, not the earlier day on which a contract for it was entered into.
GIVEN `the date when the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred` IS A DATE
      `the earlier date on which the contract in pursuance of which it was made or incurred was entered into` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 369(5)(a) the date from which interest runs` MEANS
    `the date when the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred`

-- src:4755 | (b) at such rate as the Secretary of State may prescribe by regulations.
@ref s 369(5)(b) The rate of interest (src:4755)
GIVEN `the rate the Secretary of State prescribes by regulations` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 369(5)(b) the rate of interest` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the rate the Secretary of State prescribes by regulations`
    WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST rate
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "at such rate as the Secretary of State may prescribe by regulations"

-- ---- s 370: enforcement of directors' liabilities by shareholder action ----------------------------------------

-- src:4765 | (3) An “authorised group” of members of a company means—
-- src:4766 | (a) the holders of not less than 5% in nominal value of the company's issued share capital,
-- src:4767 | (b) if the company is not limited by shares, not less than 5% of its members, or
-- src:4768 | (c) not less than 50 of the company's members.
@ref s 370(3) An authorised group (src:4765-4768)
-- (a) holders of not less than 5% in nominal value of the issued share capital; (b) if the company is not limited by shares,
-- not less than 5% of its members; (c) not less than 50 of the company's members.
GIVEN `the nominal value of the issued share capital held by the members in the group` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the company's issued share capital` IS A NUMBER
      `s 3(2) the company is limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members in the group` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members of the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(3) the members are an authorised group` MEANS
    IF    (`the nominal value of the company's issued share capital` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the nominal value of the issued share capital held by the members in the group` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `the nominal value of the company's issued share capital`)
       OR ((NOT `s 3(2) the company is limited by shares`) AND `the number of members of the company` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the number of members in the group` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `the number of members of the company`)
       OR `the number of members in the group` AT LEAST 50
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An “authorised group” of members of a company means"

-- src:4759 | (1) Any liability of a director under section 369 is enforceable—
-- src:4760 | (a) in the case of a liability of a director of a company to that company, by proceedings brought under this section in the name of the company by an authorised group of its members;
@ref s 370(1)(a) Liability of a director to the company: shareholder action in the company's name (src:4759-4760)
GIVEN `the liability is a liability of a director of the company to that company under section 369` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 370(3) the members are an authorised group` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(1)(a) the liability is enforceable in the name of the company by the group` MEANS
    IF `the liability is a liability of a director of the company to that company under section 369` AND (`s 370(3) the members are an authorised group` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by proceedings brought under this section in the name of the company by an authorised group of its members"

-- src:4761 | (b) in the case of a liability of a director of a holding company to a subsidiary, by proceedings brought under this section in the name of the subsidiary by—
-- src:4762 | (i) an authorised group of members of the subsidiary, or
-- src:4763 | (ii) an authorised group of members of the holding company.
@ref s 370(1)(b) Liability of a director of a holding company to a subsidiary: shareholder action in the subsidiary's name (src:4761-4763)
GIVEN `the liability is a liability of a director of a holding company to a subsidiary under section 369` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the members are an authorised group of members of the subsidiary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the members are an authorised group of members of the holding company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(1)(b) the liability is enforceable in the name of the subsidiary by the group` MEANS
    IF `the liability is a liability of a director of a holding company to a subsidiary under section 369` AND (`s 362 helper either answer` `the members are an authorised group of members of the subsidiary` `the members are an authorised group of members of the holding company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by an authorised group of members of the subsidiary, or an authorised group of members of the holding company"

-- src:4764 | (2) This is in addition to the right of the company to which the liability is owed to bring proceedings itself to enforce the liability.
@ref s 370(2) The company's own right to bring proceedings (src:4764)
GIVEN `the liability is owed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(2) the company may itself bring proceedings to enforce the liability` MEANS
    IF `the liability is owed to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the right of the company to which the liability is owed"

-- src:4769 | (4) The right to bring proceedings under this section is subject to the provisions of section 371.
@ref s 370(4) The right is subject to section 371 (src:4769)
GIVEN `s 370(1) the liability is enforceable in the name of the company or subsidiary by the group` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 371(1) the notice requirements are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(4) the group may bring proceedings under section 370` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The right to bring proceedings under this section is subject to the provisions of section 371" (section 371(1): "may not bring proceedings ... unless")
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 370(1) the liability is enforceable in the name of the company or subsidiary by the group` `s 371(1) the notice requirements are met`

-- src:4770 | (5) Nothing in this section affects any right of a member of a company to bring or continue proceedings under Part 11 (derivative claims or proceedings).
@ref s 370(5) Part 11 derivative claims unaffected (src:4770)
GIVEN `s 260 the member has the right to bring or continue proceedings under Part 11` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(5) the member's right to bring or continue proceedings under Part 11 is unaffected` MEANS
    IF `s 260 the member has the right to bring or continue proceedings under Part 11` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection only saves a right the member has under Part 11

-- ---- s 371: supplementary -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4772 | (1) A group of members may not bring proceedings under section 370 in the name of a company unless—
-- src:4773 | (a) the group has given written notice to the company stating—
-- src:4774 | (i) the cause of action and a summary of the facts on which the proceedings are to be based,
-- src:4775 | (ii) the names and addresses of the members comprising the group, and
-- src:4776 | (iii) the grounds on which it is alleged that those members constitute an authorised group; and
-- src:4777 | (b) not less than 28 days have elapsed between the date of the giving of the notice to the company and the bringing of the proceedings.
@ref s 371(1) The notice requirements before proceedings under section 370 (src:4772-4777)
-- "not less than 28 days have elapsed between the date of the giving of the notice to the company and the bringing of the proceedings".
GIVEN `the group has given written notice to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the cause of action and a summary of the facts on which the proceedings are to be based` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the names and addresses of the members comprising the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the grounds on which it is alleged that those members constitute an authorised group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the giving of the notice to the company` IS A DATE
      `the date of the bringing of the proceedings` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 371(1) the notice requirements are met` MEANS
    IF    `the group has given written notice to the company`
      AND `the notice states the cause of action and a summary of the facts on which the proceedings are to be based`
      AND `the notice states the names and addresses of the members comprising the group`
      AND `the notice states the grounds on which it is alleged that those members constitute an authorised group`
      AND `the date of the bringing of the proceedings` MINUS `the date of the giving of the notice to the company` AT LEAST 28
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A group of members may not bring proceedings under section 370 in the name of a company unless"

DECLARE `s 371(2) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 371(2)(a) the unauthorised amount has been made good to the company`
    `s 371(2)(b) proceedings to enforce the liability have been brought, and are being pursued with due diligence, by the company`
    `s 371(2)(c) the members proposing to bring proceedings do not constitute an authorised group`
    `s 371(2) some other ground`

-- src:4778 | (2) Where such a notice is given to a company, any director of the company may apply to the court within the period of 28 days beginning with the date of the giving of the notice for an order directing that the proposed proceedings shall not be brought, on one or more of the following grounds—
-- src:4779 | (a) that the unauthorised amount has been made good to the company;
-- src:4780 | (b) that proceedings to enforce the liability have been brought, and are being pursued with due diligence, by the company;
-- src:4781 | (c) that the members proposing to bring proceedings under this section do not constitute an authorised group.
@ref s 371(2) A director's application to the court (src:4778-4781)
-- "within the period of 28 days beginning with the date of the giving of the notice": the last day is the date of the notice plus 27.
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice has been given to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the giving of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE
      ground IS A `s 371(2) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 371(2) the director may apply to the court for an order that the proposed proceedings shall not be brought` MEANS
    IF NOT `notice has been given to the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where such a notice is given to a company"
    ELSE IF NOT `the person is a director of the company`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any director of the company may apply"
         ELSE IF `the date of the application` LESS THAN `the date of the giving of the notice` OR `the date of the application` GREATER THAN `the date of the giving of the notice` PLUS 27
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the period of 28 days beginning with the date of the giving of the notice"
              ELSE CONSIDER ground
                   WHEN `s 371(2) some other ground` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on one or more of the following grounds"
                   OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:4782 | (3) Where an application is made on the ground mentioned in subsection (2)(b), the court may as an alternative to directing that the proposed proceedings under section 370 are not to be brought, direct—
-- src:4783 | (a) that such proceedings may be brought on such terms and conditions as the court thinks fit, and
-- src:4784 | (b) that the proceedings brought by the company—
-- src:4785 | (i) shall be discontinued, or
-- src:4786 | (ii) may be continued on such terms and conditions as the court thinks fit.
@ref s 371(3) The court's alternative directions (src:4782-4786)
GIVEN `an application is made on the ground mentioned in subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 371(3) the court may make the alternative directions` MEANS
    IF `an application is made on the ground mentioned in subsection (2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application is made on the ground mentioned in subsection (2)(b)"

-- src:4787 | (4) The members by whom proceedings are brought under section 370 owe to the company in whose name they are brought the same duties in relation to the proceedings as would be owed by the company's directors if the proceedings were being brought by the company.
-- src:4788 | But proceedings to enforce any such duty may be brought by the company only with the permission of the court.
@ref s 371(4) Duties of the members who bring proceedings (src:4787-4788)
GIVEN `proceedings are brought under section 370 in the name of the company by the members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 371(4) the members owe the company the same duties as the directors would owe` MEANS
    IF `proceedings are brought under section 370 in the name of the company by the members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members by whom proceedings are brought under section 370"

-- src:4788 | But proceedings to enforce any such duty may be brought by the company only with the permission of the court.
@ref s 371(4) Proceedings by the company to enforce those duties (src:4788)
GIVEN `the court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 371(4) the company may bring proceedings to enforce those duties` MEANS
    IF `the court has given permission`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be brought by the company only with the permission of the court"

-- src:4789 | (5) Proceedings brought under section 370 may not be discontinued or settled by the group except with the permission of the court, which may be given on such terms as the court thinks fit.
@ref s 371(5) Discontinuance or settlement (src:4789)
GIVEN `the court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 371(5) the group may discontinue or settle the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the court has given permission`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be discontinued or settled by the group except with the permission of the court"

-- ---- s 372: costs of shareholder action -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4791 | (1) This section applies in relation to proceedings brought under section 370 in the name of a company (“the company”) by an authorised group (“the group”).
@ref s 372(1) Where section 372 applies (src:4791)
GIVEN `proceedings are brought under section 370 in the name of a company by an authorised group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(1) section 372 applies to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `proceedings are brought under section 370 in the name of a company by an authorised group`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to proceedings brought under section 370 in the name of a company"

-- src:4792 | (2) The group may apply to the court for an order directing the company to indemnify the group in respect of costs incurred or to be incurred by the group in connection with the proceedings.
-- src:4793 | The court may make such an order on such terms as it thinks fit.
@ref s 372(2) An order that the company indemnify the group for costs (src:4792-4793)
GIVEN `s 372(1) section 372 applies to the proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(2) the group may apply for an order that the company indemnify the group in respect of costs` MEANS
    IF `s 372(1) section 372 applies to the proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the application is for the group whose proceedings section 372 covers

-- src:4794 | (3) The group is not entitled to be paid any such costs out of the assets of the company except by virtue of such an order.
@ref s 372(3) No costs out of the company's assets except under an order (src:4794)
GIVEN `an order under subsection (2) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(3) the group is entitled to be paid costs out of the assets of the company` MEANS
    IF `an order under subsection (2) has been made`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement is "by virtue of such an order", whose terms are the court's
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The group is not entitled to be paid any such costs out of the assets of the company except by virtue of such an order"

-- src:4795 | (4) If no such order has been made with respect to the proceedings, then—
-- src:4796 | (a) if the company is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that costs incurred by the company in connection with the proceedings should be paid by any defendant, the costs shall be paid to the group; and
@ref s 372(4)(a) Costs awarded to the company or agreed to be paid by a defendant (src:4795-4796)
GIVEN `an order under subsection (2) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that costs incurred by the company should be paid by any defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(4)(a) the costs shall be paid to the group` MEANS
    IF (NOT `an order under subsection (2) has been made`) AND `the company is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that costs incurred by the company should be paid by any defendant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no such order has been made with respect to the proceedings, then— (a) if the company is awarded costs"

-- src:4795 | (4) If no such order has been made with respect to the proceedings, then—
-- src:4796 | (a) if the company is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that costs incurred by the company in connection with the proceedings should be paid by any defendant, the costs shall be paid to the group; and
-- src:4797 | (b) if any defendant is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that any defendant should be paid costs incurred by him in connection with the proceedings, the costs shall be paid by the group.
@ref s 372(4)(b) Costs awarded to a defendant or agreed to be paid to a defendant (src:4795-4797)
GIVEN `an order under subsection (2) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any defendant is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that any defendant should be paid costs incurred by him in connection with the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(4)(b) the costs shall be paid by the group` MEANS
    IF (NOT `an order under subsection (2) has been made`) AND `any defendant is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that any defendant should be paid costs incurred by him in connection with the proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no such order has been made with respect to the proceedings, then— (b) if any defendant is awarded costs"

-- (5): a rule of reading: in Scotland, read "expenses" for "costs" and "defender" for "defendant".
-- src:4798 | (5) In the application of this section to Scotland for “costs” read “expenses” and for “defendant” read “defender”.
@ref s 372(5) Scotland: "expenses" for "costs" and "defender" for "defendant" (src:4798)
GIVEN `the section is applied to Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 372(5) the word to read for costs` MEANS
    IF `the section is applied to Scotland`
    THEN JUST "expenses"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the application of this section to Scotland"

-- src:4798 | (5) In the application of this section to Scotland for “costs” read “expenses” and for “defendant” read “defender”.
@ref s 372(5) Scotland: "expenses" for "costs" and "defender" for "defendant" (src:4798)
GIVEN `the section is applied to Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 372(5) the word to read for defendant` MEANS
    IF `the section is applied to Scotland`
    THEN JUST "defender"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the application of this section to Scotland"

-- ---- s 373: information for purposes of shareholder action ---------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4800 | (1) Where proceedings have been brought under section 370 in the name of a company by an authorised group, the group is entitled to require the company to provide it with all information relating to the subject matter of the proceedings that is in the company's possession or under its control or which is reasonably obtainable by it.
@ref s 373(1) The group's entitlement to information (src:4800)
GIVEN `proceedings have been brought under section 370 in the name of the company by an authorised group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to the subject matter of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is in the company's possession or under its control or is reasonably obtainable by it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(1) the group is entitled to require the company to provide the information` MEANS
    IF NOT `proceedings have been brought under section 370 in the name of the company by an authorised group`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where proceedings have been brought under section 370 in the name of a company by an authorised group"
    ELSE IF `the information relates to the subject matter of the proceedings` AND `the information is in the company's possession or under its control or is reasonably obtainable by it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all information relating to the subject matter of the proceedings that is in the company's possession or under its control or which is reasonably obtainable by it"

-- src:4801 | (2) If the company, having been required by the group to do so, refuses to provide the group with all or any of that information, the court may, on an application made by the group, make an order directing—
-- src:4802 | (a) the company, and
-- src:4803 | (b) any of its officers or employees specified in the application,
-- src:4804 | to provide the group with the information in question in such form and by such means as the court may direct.
@ref s 373(2) The court's order for information (src:4801-4804)
GIVEN `the company, having been required by the group to do so, refuses to provide all or any of that information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group has applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(2) the court may order the company and specified officers or employees to provide the information` MEANS
    IF `the company, having been required by the group to do so, refuses to provide all or any of that information` AND `the group has applied to the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company, having been required by the group to do so, refuses to provide the group with all or any of that information, the court may, on an application made by the group"
